<%# One broadcast: the whole state of the match as one message, rendered for one audience.

    Called by MatchBroadcasts#broadcast_state! once per audience (the Red seat, the White seat
    and everybody else) after every accepted action, and delivered to that audience's signed
    Turbo stream. The acting browser's own response carries the same fragments from
    matches/update.turbo_stream.erb, so nothing here is the only path to anything.

    All five fragments go in one message rather than five, so a page can never show a board
    from one action beside a move list from another.

    Rendered outside a request: no Current, no session, no cookies, no request helpers, and no
    _url helpers (there is no host). Everything comes from the three locals. The invite panel
    is rendered without a link on purpose, which empties it: a match that has just been joined
    or cancelled has no invite left to show, and those are the only broadcasts a waiting match
    ever makes. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Match::BOARD_ID, partial: "matches/board",
      locals: { match: match, game: game, selected: nil, seats: seats } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Match::STATUS_ID, partial: "matches/status",
      locals: { match: match, game: game } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Match::INVITE_ID, partial: "matches/invite",
      locals: { match: match, seats: seats, link: nil } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Match::MOVES_ID, partial: "matches/moves",
      locals: { pairs: move_pairs(game), highlight: game.plies } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Match::CONTROLS_ID, partial: "matches/controls",
      locals: { match: match, game: game, seats: seats } %>
